# Native agent-device action sections; suite.json composes guards and includes.
# settings-guide

# section open-settings
press "${TARGET}"

# section settings-arrived
is visible "${TARGET}"

# section seek
# The row is in ABOUT, which is the last card on the page and below the fold on
# every phone -- and the page does not even build ABOUT until it has been idle
# once (`deep` in `settings.tsx`), so the first flick is also what proves the
# deferred half of the screen arrived at all. A flick rather than a pan: the
# target is a full two-line row, so an overshoot still leaves it in the tree for
# the scroll-to-visible loop to come back to. The 13pt instrument labels in
# `flows/settings.ad` are the case that needs `gesture pan`; this is not one.
scroll down --pixels 320

# section row-visible
# Asserted and not pressed. The row hands the reader to a browser, and a flow
# that taps it leaves the app under test -- on a shared QA device, with no way
# back that does not depend on whatever browser the image happens to have.
# What this flow owns is that Settings offers the guide; that the address is an
# https page on muqun.dev is `src/constants/__tests__/links.test.ts`.
is visible "${TARGET}"
